menu "natVR Transport"

choice NATVR_TRANSPORT
    prompt "natVR transport"
    default NATVR_TRANSPORT_WIRELESS
    help
        Selects how EMG frames leave the device. This seeds the runtime transport
        mode at boot (see TransportMode in main/main.cpp). It is a build-time
        choice: switching modes is a rebuild + reflash, not a live booth flip.

config NATVR_TRANSPORT_WIRELESS
    bool "Wireless (WiFi/MQTT)"
    help
        Primary path: publish every frame over WiFi/MQTT. Serial off. This is
        today's default and normal operation on good RF.

config NATVR_TRANSPORT_AUTO
    bool "Auto (wireless, serial fallback)"
    help
        Wireless-first: publish over MQTT while connected, and transparently fall
        back to the USB-serial console only while MQTT is down (debounced), then
        return to MQTT when it recovers. Recommended for the convention booth --
        it self-manages with no operator action.

config NATVR_TRANSPORT_SERIAL
    bool "Serial (USB backup)"
    help
        Force the wired USB-serial path; WiFi/NTP/MQTT are never brought up. Use
        on known-bad RF. Pair with the host shim (natvr-serial-bridge).

endchoice

endmenu
